  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=v(t)$ over $[0,40].$ \nIn this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the total distance can be approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈v(7)Δ{t}_{1}+v(15)Δ{t}_{2}+v(25)Δ{t}_{3}+v(32)Δ{t}_{4}+v(40)Δ{t}_{5},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δt$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $7$ | $15$ | $25$ | $32$ | $40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δt$ | $-$ | $7$ | $8$ | $10$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| $v(t)$ | $-$ | $10$ | $25$ | $40$ | $46$ | $49$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the number of liters and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈10\\cdot 7+25\\cdot 8+40\\cdot 10+46\\cdot 7+49\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =70+200+400+322+392 \\\\  & =1\\,384.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance covered by the drone. So, the distance is approximately $1\\,384$ feet.",
